# xftest1.input — click the only button, which makes the program exit.
#
# Coordinates are surface-relative, i.e. relative to the client's own surface.
# The headless compositor implements no window placement: each toplevel surface
# covers the canvas on its own, so the 230x100 form's surface is 230x100 and the
# button at (20,20) 190x60 has its centre at (115,50).  (XForms asks for the
# window to be centred on the pointer -- FL_PLACE_MOUSE -- which moves the *X*
# window inside the synthetic root, but the pointer coordinates the compositor
# sends are still surface-relative.)
#
# There is deliberately no trailing "screenshot": the compositor exits the
# instant it takes one, closing the Wayland connection while the client may still
# be processing the click, and the client would die of XIO rather than of its own
# accord.  The script just ends, and the runner checks that the client exited 0.

motion 115 50
sleep 300
button press left
sleep 200
button release left
sleep 800